A||N||18||grinthock||My Fiero Drove Me EXCITEMENT this morn!||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||10-08-2001||10:15 AM||||Gosh, why the hell am I posting this, except to say this morning I have never loved my car more.<P>It's a beautiful (yet cool probably 10 deg C, or 45 deg F,) sunny day here, cool air, slight moisture in the air, VERY clear.<P>I decided to take the car for a spin.<P>There is something to be said about running your fiero for 12 hrs STRAIGHT at 2500 RPM, that's what I did coming to and from the PA Tech Day (see the awesome threads), and now the car runs AMAZING. <P>But back to the story.  I took her out onto some "Fiero Friendly" roads (reference, yeah I was robbed!), and then onto the highway (I almost typed interstate!) and WOW she is driving NICE... Sounds AMAZING, drives GREAT!  Handles like a dream.  I love my fiero.  <P>It was a great drive, not many people around, no perspective races (nor did I really want any), just a nice drive with some tunes. <P>That's it.  She's there for me, outside my window I can see her now.  Maybe later her and I will take to the roads again.  Perhaps with the company of another Fiero, and then later perhaps, in the rear view mirror we will see yes, not 1, but many imports.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||10-08-2001||11:05 AM||||For me it's all that and "Radar Love" by Golden Earring on the radio!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks for sharing,<P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||14
